    "knowledge_point": "Computing the Variance Given the Number, Sum, and Sum of Squares of the Data Points",
    "problem": "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of a data set ${x}_{i}$ consisting of $7$ data points, where\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}=35,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}^{2}=201.\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance of the data set is given by \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=7$ points in our data set, and we know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}=35,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 35 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ We know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}^{2}=201,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 201 \\\\  & =\\frac{201}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{201}{7}-{(5)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{201}{7}-25 \\\\  & =\\frac{201-175}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
